---
import Page from '@layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy & Terms of Use"
  description="How Harmony Immigration Services collects, uses, and protects your personal information, and the terms that apply when you use our website and services."
>
  <section class="pt-16 pb-24 md:pt-24 md:pb-32">
    <div class="container">
      <a id="assessment-back-link" href="#" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold mb-6" style="color:#55BFC0; display:none;">
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M19 12H5M11 18l-6-6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        Back to assessment
      </a>
      <div class="reveal max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="mt-5">Privacy Policy &amp; Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-left">
          Harmony Immigration Services ("we", "us", "our") respects your privacy. This page explains what personal and sensitive information we collect when you use our website, complete an assessment, contact us, or engage our services; why we collect it; how we use it; how we protect it; and the terms that apply when you use this website or our services.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal prose-content mx-auto mt-16 max-w-3xl">
        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>
          When you submit an enquiry, booking, or visa assessment form, or contact us directly, we collect the information you choose to provide. This may include your name, email address, phone number, and information about your circumstances or immigration enquiry.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where necessary to assess your visa eligibility or provide immigration advice or services, we may also collect sensitive information. This may include information about your health, character or criminal history, immigration and visa history, previous applications or refusals, and other personal circumstances relevant to your immigration matter.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may receive this information through our website forms, during consultations, in documents you provide, or when you communicate with us directly, including by email.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <p>We use your personal and sensitive information only where reasonably necessary to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>respond to your enquiries;</li>
          <li>assess your circumstances and potential eligibility for a visa or immigration pathway;</li>
          <li>provide the immigration advice or services you request;</li>
          <li>communicate with you about your case, appointments, or documentation; and</li>
          <li>meet our legal and professional obligations as a licensed immigration adviser.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Sensitive information submitted as part of a visa assessment is used to understand your circumstances and assess your potential visa options. Your personal and sensitive information is not used for marketing purposes or to train AI models.
        </p>

        <h2>Who can access your information</h2>
        <p>
          Information submitted through our visa assessment process is sent to Harmony Immigration and reviewed by our advisers. Your assessment is not automatically evaluated by a system, and you will not receive an automatic eligibility result.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal or sensitive information or share it with third parties for marketing or unrelated purposes. If you engage Harmony Immigration to provide immigration services, relevant information may be shared with immigration authorities or other parties where necessary to provide those services, where you have authorised us to do so, or where disclosure is required or permitted by law.
        </p>

        <h2>No automated visa decisions</h2>
        <p>
          Information you provide through our visa assessment does not result in an automated decision about your visa eligibility. Your answers are reviewed by a Harmony Immigration adviser. No automated system makes the final assessment of your circumstances or determines whether you are eligible for a visa.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep your information</h2>
        <p>
          We keep information submitted through our enquiry and visa assessment forms for 7 years. After this period, the information is securely deleted.
        </p>

        <h2>How we protect your information</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect the personal and sensitive information we hold from unauthorised access, use, disclosure, alteration, or loss. Access to your information is limited to those who need it for the purpose for which it was collected or to provide the services you have requested.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You may ask to see or correct the personal information we hold about you. You may also contact us to request deletion of information where applicable. To make a request or ask a question about how we handle your information, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@harmony-immigration.com">info@harmony-immigration.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Terms of use</h2>
        <p>By using this website or engaging our services, you agree to the following terms.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Advice and services.</strong> Any general information provided on this website is for guidance only and does not constitute formal immigration advice. Formal advice is only given once we have reviewed your specific circumstances as part of a paid engagement.</li>
          <li><strong>No client relationship.</strong> Submitting an enquiry, booking, or assessment form does not create a client relationship with Harmony Immigration. A client relationship begins only once we have agreed to act for you.</li>
          <li><strong>No guaranteed outcomes.</strong> While we work diligently on every case, immigration decisions are made by the relevant government authorities. We cannot guarantee the outcome of any application.</li>
          <li><strong>Website content.</strong> This website and its content are provided "as is". We make reasonable efforts to keep information accurate and up to date but do not warrant that all content is complete or error-free.</li>
          <li><strong>Your agreement.</strong> By submitting an enquiry, booking, or assessment form on this website, you agree to this Privacy Policy and these Terms of Use.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-neutral-400)]">
          Last updated: 2026. If you have any questions about this policy, please <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<script>
  const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
  const returnTo = params.get('returnTo');
  if (params.get('from') === 'assessment' && returnTo) {
    const link = document.getElementById('assessment-back-link') as HTMLAnchorElement | null;
    if (link) {
      link.href = returnTo;
      link.style.display = 'inline-flex';
    }
  }
</script>
